WEBVTT - SWID-SHRK Aerospace & Mechanics Laboratory
Title: Strut Antiprism Modeling — Part 3
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Welcome to Part 3: Finite element mesh discretization, hourglass suppression, and explicit general self-contact formulation.

2
00:08.000 --> 00:22.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>In the Mesh Module, seed the strut edges with an element size of 0.75 mm, giving approximately 40 elements per diagonal member to capture localized plastic hinge formation.

3
00:22.000 --> 00:36.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>For solid representations, select C3D8R 8-node linear brick elements with reduced integration. For beam representations, use B31 Timoshenko beams.

4
00:36.000 --> 00:52.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Under Element Type, enable Enhanced Hourglass Control. This is mandatory in Abaqus/Explicit to prevent unphysical zero-energy hourglass modes during severe strut plastic collapse.

5
00:52.000 --> 01:08.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Move to the Interaction Module. Create an Abaqus/Explicit General Contact interaction spanning all exterior surfaces of the metamaterial.

6
01:08.000 --> 01:25.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Assign Tangential Behavior with penalty friction coefficient mu = 0.20, and Normal Behavior with "Hard" contact pressure-overclosure. This models realistic strut-on-strut compaction.

7
01:25.000 --> 01:38.000
<v Dr. Pouria Hejazi>Check mesh verification: confirm zero aspect-ratio warnings and verify that all contact pairs are properly recognized for dynamic crushing.
